From c1068a82ab79281c2723bd079dc1b200c249f8fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kiln <kiln@localhost>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:18:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] vo_libmpv/gpu-next: hardware decoding through ra_hwdec

The gpu-next render backend created hwdec devices but never loaded an
interop, so every hwdec mode fell back to software. Load the interops on
an ra_pl over the backend's pl_gpu, map hardware frames through a
ra_hwdec_mapper slot as vo_gpu_next does, and let hwdec_vulkan take its
device from pl_vulkan when there is no mpv Vulkan swapchain (an imported
host device).
---
 video/out/gpu_next/libmpv_gpu_next.c |   3 +-
 video/out/gpu_next/video.c           | 173 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 video/out/gpu_next/video.h           |   3 +
 video/out/hwdec/hwdec_vulkan.c       |  63 +++++-----
 4 files changed, 206 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)

diff --git a/video/out/gpu_next/libmpv_gpu_next.c b/video/out/gpu_next/libmpv_gpu_next.c
